## What I implemented

`list_ops.py` now implements all 8 operations from `pass` stubs, honoring the prompt's "without using existing functions" (no `len`/`map`/`filter`/`sum`/`reduce`/`reversed`/slicing — everything is hand-rolled loops + list concatenation):

- `append`/`concat`/`filter`/`map`/`length` — explicit iteration
- `foldl`/`foldr` — both call `function(acc, item)`; `foldr` traverses right-to-left via a manual `reverse` (the order note in the prompt)
- `reverse` — prepend build (no `[::-1]`, no flattening)

